{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Goal\n\nRemove the legacy `rebar reconcile --mode reconcile-check` CLI/direct-engine command and its persisted `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` artifact without breaking the canonical bridge surfaces that replaced its observables.\n\nThe replacement is intentionally distributed:\n- `rebar bridge preview` is the live Jira-vs-local differ/proposed-change observable.\n- `rebar bridge fsck --output json` is the offline orphan/unbound/binding-drift audit observable.\n- `rebar bridge status --json` remains the status surface, but must stop reading the stale legacy `reconcile-check.json` artifact once the writer is deleted.\n\nThe pause sentinel string `gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"` is not the CLI command and must be preserved byte-for-byte.\n\n## Scope\n\nRemove the CLI/direct-engine reconcile-check command path and every caller owned by this ticket:\n\n- `src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py`: repoint the retained `reconcile-check` runner profile to canonical `rebar bridge preview`, not `bridge fsck`.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py`: remove the legacy top-level `rebar reconcile` route registration.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/reconcile.py`: remove legacy `--mode reconcile-check` parser exposure and the `--filter-local-ids` CLI surface.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/help/reconcile.txt`: remove generated/static help for the removed legacy CLI surface.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`: delete `_run_reconcile_check`, the `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK` dispatch branch, and the CLI-only `filter_local_ids` handoff on this route.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/request.py`: remove legacy-route `--mode reconcile-check` and `--filter-local-ids` parsing; keep canonical `preview`/`sync` normalization.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/mode.py`: remove `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK`, its `_ORDERED` entry, and its `MODE_CAPS` entry.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_preflight.py`: remove reconcile-check from no-write/preflight logic and docs.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py`: remove `_read_reconcile_diagnostics()` and stop surfacing `reconcile_diagnostics` from the retired artifact.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_check.py`: delete the orphaned legacy report module.\n- Update stale in-code comments/docstrings in `binding_recovery.py`, `binding_walk.py`, `fetcher.py`, `get_rotation.py`, `load_phase.py`, `pass_support.py`, `reconcile_helpers.py`, and `ticket_planner.py` so no-write wording refers to `dry-run`/`preview`.\n- Migrate CI/probe callers and the `bridge status` schema/typing: `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`, `Jenkinsfile`, `scripts/jira-pressure-test/e2e_field_validation_probe.sh`, `scripts/jira-pressure-test/e2e_validation_probe.sh` (invoke `bridge preview` for live discrepancy, `bridge fsck --output json` for orphan/unbound audits), and remove the now-unsourced `reconcile_diagnostics` field from `src/rebar/schemas/bridge_status.schema.json` and its `BridgeStatus` typing in `src/rebar/types.py`.\n- Update `docs` and `CHANGELOG.md`, and update/remove tests exercising the deleted command/module; add regression coverage for the canonical replacements and pause-sentinel preservation.\n\n## Design Decisions\n\n1. `bridge fsck` is not the sole replacement for `reconcile-check`. It is an offline audit over committed event/binding state and can intentionally exit `1` for audit findings; it does not provide the live Jira-vs-local discrepancy report or legacy success semantics.\n2. `_bridge_runner.py` must map the retained `reconcile-check` profile to `rebar bridge preview`. The runner treats nonzero provider exits as operational failures and skips delivery, so mapping to `bridge fsck` would make ordinary fsck findings look like runner failures.\n3. `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json` has no canonical writer after `_run_reconcile_check` is deleted. Do not invent a new writer. Remove the `last_pass.py` reader so `bridge status` cannot report stale diagnostics.\n4. Preserve `_ref_lock.py` pause documents exactly: `gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"` remains the live pause sentinel, semantically distinct from the removed CLI command.\n5. Do not remove dead internal `filter_local_ids` engine plumbing beyond this ticket's CLI surface; that cleanup belongs to follow-up `f8c4-ac9b-42c5-4bb0`.\n6. Do not edit `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py` or `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`; public Python/MCP `rebar.reconcile(mode=...)` compatibility belonged to sibling `c195-03cd-fc03-4ae0`, which landed first.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_mode.py` proves `Mode.RECONCILE_CHECK`, `_ORDERED[\"reconcile-check\"]`, and `MODE_CAPS[RECONCILE_CHECK]` are gone while dry-run/bootstrap/live ordering still works.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py` proves `python -m rebar_reconciler --mode reconcile-check` is rejected as unknown and `_run_reconcile_check` is no longer dispatched.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py` proves `_bridge_runner.MODE_COMMANDS[\"reconcile-check\"]` invokes `rebar bridge preview`, preserves runner delivery semantics, and does not map to `bridge fsck`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py` proves orphaned bindings, orphaned Jira, unbound local, and unbound Jira remain available through canonical `bridge fsck --output json`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_heldout.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_relocated_store.py` proves `bridge status` still reports last-pass/pause/live-lock status but no longer reads or surfaces stale `.bridge_state/reconcile-check.json`.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_advisory_lock_ref_backend.py` proves pause documents still preserve `gated_mode == \"reconcile-check\"` byte-for-byte.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/test_reconcile_check_cli_removal_heldout.py` is the held-out oracle proving the removed CLI spelling is rejected, the canonical replacement guidance is present, and `git grep \"reconcile-check\" -- src/rebar tests docs .github Jenkinsfile scripts` only finds the preserved pause sentinel or documented historical/changelog references.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint` passes.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck` passes.\n- [ ] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make test` passes.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe held-out oracle is `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_reconcile_check_cli_removal_heldout.py` (deleted command stays deleted; `_bridge_runner` points to `bridge preview`; pause-sentinel files excluded from removal). Each Acceptance Criterion above names its own proving `pytest` command; full gates are `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test`, all run with the worktree `.venv/bin` first on PATH.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Do not edit `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py` or `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` (c195 owns Python/MCP `rebar.reconcile(mode=...)`).\n- Do not remove engine `filter_local_ids` plumbing beyond the CLI surface (follow-up `f8c4-ac9b-42c5-4bb0`).\n- Do not change `_ref_lock.py` pause sentinel bytes or pause document schema.\n- Do not change canonical `bridge preview`/`sync`/`fsck`/`status` semantics except removing stale `reconcile_diagnostics` file consumption."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788531082550055309,"uuid":"ab9fac58-ea59-4432-966c-6bb7724dd907"}